  "equipment_type": "Pulse meter data recorder (meter interface)",
  "applies_to": "E-Mon D-Mon IDR-8 and IDR-16 interval data recorders (pulse-input meter recorders) on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the E-Mon IDR-8/IDR-16: 64 objects (32 AI, 32 AO), all polled. For each of 16 channels it has usage (pulse count) and pulse value as outputs and demand and demand pulse value as inputs. Channels 9-16 apply to the IDR-16 only.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile E_Mon_D_Mon_IDR8_IDR16_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/E_Mon_d_Mon_IDR8_IDR16.doc).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "All 64 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile E_Mon_D_Mon_IDPR8_IDPR16_a",
    "doc_number": "E_Mon_D_Mon_IDR8_IDR16_a_LX.csv",
